---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import posterImage from '../assets/hanoi-poster.png';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

import '../styles/theme.css';
import '../styles/global.css';

const blogPost =
  'https://tarheels.live/globalhealth/2026/10/01/serious-work-silly-coffee-wrapping-up-in-hanoi/';

const posterPdf = '/posters/hanoi-prep-practicum-day-2026.pdf';

const facts = [
  ['Host', 'Center for Research and Training on Substance Use-HIV (CREATA-H), Hanoi Medical University'],
  ['Site', 'Sexual Health Promotion Clinic, Hanoi'],
  ['When', 'June – July 2026'],
  ['Design', 'Negative-binomial interrupted time series'],
  ['Data', 'Seven years of clinic records · 86 monthly observations · ~11,000 clients'],
  ['Tools', 'R, REDCap, Stata'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="PEPFAR funding withdrawal and PrEP services in Hanoi — Liam Powell"
  description="MPH practicum at Hanoi Medical University: an interrupted time series analysis of seven years of clinic records, estimating what the 2025 PEPFAR/CDC funding withdrawal did to PrEP services."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <article class="study">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="study-head">
          <p class="study-kicker">MPH practicum · Hanoi, Vietnam · Summer 2026</p>
          <h1 class="study-title">
            Measuring what the PEPFAR funding withdrawal did to PrEP services at a Hanoi clinic
          </h1>
          <p class="study-award">Practicum Excellence Award, 2026 · UNC Gillings</p>
          <p class="study-lede">
            In 2025, PEPFAR/CDC funding for PrEP, the daily medication that prevents HIV, was
            withdrawn from a sexual health clinic in Hanoi. The staff were too busy keeping the
            program running to measure what changed. For my practicum I designed and ran the
            analysis that did.
          </p>
        </header>

        <dl class="study-facts">
          {facts.map(([term, detail]) => (
            <div class="fact">
              <dt>{term}</dt>
              <dd>{detail}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>

        <div class="study-body">
          <h2>The question</h2>
          <p>
            The team at CREATA-H handed me a research question rather than a task list: what did
            the funding withdrawal do to PrEP initiation, medication dispensing, and service use
            at the clinic, which serves a population that is predominantly men who have sex with
            men? The study design was mine to work out.
          </p>

          <h2>Starting from the clinic's own numbers</h2>
          <p>
            The data were seven years of clinic records exported from REDCap: 86 monthly
            observations covering about 11,000 clients. The clinic already reported monthly
            counts from this database using its own Stata definitions. Before modeling anything,
            I rebuilt those definitions in R until my pipeline reproduced the clinic's internal
            monthly counts exactly. The analysis then started from figures the clinic recognized
            as its own.
          </p>

          <h2>The design</h2>
          <p>
            I used a negative-binomial interrupted time series: a count model fitted to the
            monthly series, with the funding withdrawal as the interruption, so that what
            happened afterward can be compared with what the earlier trend would have predicted.
          </p>
          <p>
            One complication shaped the analysis. A research cohort was running at the clinic
            over the same period, and left in the counts it would have masked the funding
            effect. I isolated the funding effect from that cohort.
          </p>

          <h2>Beyond the dataset</h2>
          <p>
            Alongside the records I had key-informant conversations with clinicians and program
            staff about how the withdrawal had affected the people who rely on the clinic and how
            the clinic itself had adapted. Those conversations shaped how I read the numbers.
          </p>

          <h2>What the clinic received</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>A results memo.</li>
            <li>
              A reproducible analysis repository with a data dictionary and automated checks
              against the clinic's own reported counts, documented so that someone else can add
              new records and rerun it.
            </li>
            <li>
              A share-out of the findings to clinic leadership, CDC, and CREATA-H investigators.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <blockquote class="study-quote">
            <p>
              “It’s easy to write something that runs once, on my data, in July. It’s harder to
              make something that someone else can pick up six months from now, add new records
              to, and adapt when the questions change.”
            </p>
            <footer>
              From <a href={blogPost} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my post on the
              Gillings Global Health blog</a>, October 2026
            </footer>
          </blockquote>

          <h2>Results</h2>
          <p>
            The estimates, figures, and limitations are on my poster for MPH Practicum Day 2026
            at UNC Gillings. <a href={posterPdf}>Open the poster (PDF, 2.9 MB)</a>,
            or <a href="mailto:william.powell@unc.edu">email me</a> if you'd like to talk
            through the findings or the methods.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="study-poster">
          <a href={posterPdf}>
            <Image
              src={posterImage}
              alt="Poster titled “When free PrEP medication ran out, visits fell by nearly two-thirds: PrEP use at Hanoi Medical University's Sexual Health Promotion clinic, 2019–2026”, with headline estimates, a chart of monthly PrEP service visits, and background, methods, results, and impact sections."
              widths={[640, 1280]}
              sizes="(min-width: 700px) 640px, 100vw"
              format="webp"
              quality={82}
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>
          <figcaption>Poster for MPH Practicum Day 2026, UNC Gillings. Select it to open the full-size PDF.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p class="study-back"><a href="/#projects">← All research &amp; projects</a></p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .study {
    padding: 4.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .study-head,
  .study-body {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .study-kicker {
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .study-title {
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .study-award {
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .study-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-subhead);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .study-facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0 3rem;
    margin: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .study-facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .fact {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .fact dt {
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .fact dd {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .study-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-heading);
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .study-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .study-body p,
  .study-body li {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .study-body p + p {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .study-body ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .study-body li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .study-quote {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  .study-quote p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-subhead);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .study-quote footer {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .study-poster {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .study-poster a {
    display: block;
  }

  .study-poster :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .study-poster figcaption {
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .study-back {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }
</style>
